<p>On September 30, 1996, President Clinton signed into law the Deposit Insurance Funds Act of 1996, which authorized a one-time deposit-insurance premium assessment by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) of 65.7 cents per $100 of deposits insured by the Savings Association Insurance Fund and held as of March 31, 1995.  ASB's assessment was $8.3 million after tax and was accrued in September 1996.</p>
